---
permalink: /site.json
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
{#- Site metadata, served as a file.

    assets/ext/js/custom.js fetches this when the Site Info buttons on
    /posts/custom-javascript/ are clicked - once with XMLHttpRequest, once
    with the Fetch API - and renders it as a list. Both handlers report a
    failure to console.error only, so without this file the buttons look
    fine and do nothing at all.

    Built with `dump` on every value rather than by quoting them inline: a
    stray quote or backslash in a setting would otherwise produce a document
    that parses as nothing. The shape matches yolo-11ty's own /site.json,
    because custom.js reads these exact keys. -#}
{
  "name": {{ settings.name | dump | safe }},
  "title": {{ settings.title | dump | safe }},
  "description": {{ settings.description | dump | safe }},
  "version": {{ (settings.version | default(build.version)) | dump | safe }},
  "brand": {
    "theme": {{ settings.brand.theme | dump | safe }},
    "syntax": {{ settings.brand.syntax | dump | safe }}
  },
  "buildDate": {{ build.date | dump | safe }}
}
